secrets/
data/
logs/
tmp/
backups/
pcloud/
ipfs/
pcloud/restore-cache/
*.log
.env
!config/mapping/photogrammetry-volume.env
config/mastodon/patches/
# Superseded 2026-10-01 by grafana-admin.env, which holds ONLY non-secret
# settings and IS tracked. The admin password moved to KDE Wallet
# (ao-admin/grafana-admin-password). Kept ignored so a reintroduced cleartext
# copy can never be committed.
config/platform/monitoring/grafana.env
ALWAYSON/secrets/
logs/operations/

# Python bytecode caches. Regenerated on every run; never belongs in the
# repository. One such file was tracked by mistake and was removed.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Timestamped backups of live unit and script files, e.g.
# ao-sales.network.BAK-20260930-161848. These are operator safety copies of
# files that still exist, not history, so they are noise in the index.
*.BAK-*

# Cross-session handoff notes (README 4.1 rule 11 companions). These are
# INTERNAL operator/agent coordination material: they name the host, the
# operator account, kernel and package versions, and open security findings.
# This repository is PUBLIC, so they must never be committed. Four of these
# files were tracked and pushed by mistake on 2026-10-01 and have been
# untracked here; see the note in the commit message. Untracking stops future
# exposure but does NOT remove them from git history.
# Moved 2026-10-10 to agents/handoffs/ when this material was consolidated
# under agents/. The old name contained SPACES, which broke `git check-ignore`
# whenever the path was quoted (git reads the quotes as part of the pattern).
# The new path has no spaces.
#
# 2026-10-10 (operator decision): the session runbooks are now TRACKED. They are
# instructions for the AI sessions, they contain no host, account or credential
# data (verified: 0 matches for user/home/IP/key patterns), and they were local
# only by accident of the blanket rule -- so the other sessions could not see
# them on GitHub.
#
# The exclusion itself REMAINS for the rest of the folder: the narrative
# handoffs still name the host, the operator account, versions and open
# security findings, and this repository is PUBLIC.
agents/HANDOFFS (BETWEEN AI AGENTS)/*
!agents/HANDOFFS (BETWEEN AI AGENTS)/SESSION ASSIGNMENTS (AI WORKGROUPS)/

# Runtime coordination folders that must never enter the index.
.playwright-mcp/
GAZEBO/worlds-run/

# Generated topology binaries. build_svg.py is the source and IS tracked;
# everything it writes is reproducible with one command, so it is not.
# Scoped to the topology folders so that assets/ keeps its committed copies
# of the README diagrams.
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - SINGLE GRAPHIC/*.png
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - SINGLE GRAPHIC/*.pdf
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - SINGLE GRAPHIC/*.svg
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - SINGLE GRAPHIC/*.html
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - SINGLE GRAPHIC/*.json
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - SINGLE GRAPHIC/bands/
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*.png
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*.pdf
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*.svg
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*.html
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*.dot
# Its subfolder of superseded v7 graphics: ignore the images by extension but
# keep the README that explains them, so the note travels with the folder.
# Extension patterns rather than "<dir>/" because git will not re-include a
# file whose parent directory is itself excluded.
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*/*.png
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*/*.pdf
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*/*.svg
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*/*.html
TOPOLOGY/TOPOLOGY - ARCHIVE/*/*.dot
